        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ad6b2934-5f41-54c0-b21e-8544cf2d3079",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Joy Formidable, Sixpence None the Richer\n- Places: North Wales, London, England, New Braunfels, Texas, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Releases: A Balloon Called Moaning, The Big Roar, A Heavy Abacus, Whirring\n- Topics: alternative rock, Christian rock, discography\n\nFacts:\n- The Joy Formidable is a Welsh alternative rock band that formed in 2007 in North Wales and is currently based in London, England.\n- A Balloon Called Moaning, the debut extended play by The Joy Formidable, was released in December 2008.\n- The Big Roar, the debut studio album by The Joy Formidable, was released in January 2011 and reached No. 31 on the UK Albums Chart.\n- Whirring and A Heavy Abacus, singles from The Big Roar by The Joy Formidable, reached No. 7 and No. 25 on the US Alternative Songs Chart, respectively.\n- A Heavy Abacus was the fifth and final single from The Big Roar by The Joy Formidable and was released in July 2011.\n- Sixpence None the Richer, also known as Sixpence, is an American alternative Christian rock band that formed in New Braunfels, Texas, and later settled in Nashville, Tennessee.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "92715bb8-7457-54b3-87b7-a5bca2de54ce",
        "text": "Page: The Joy Formidable. Sentence: The Joy Formidable is a Welsh alternative rock band, formed in 2007 in North Wales and currently based in London, England.\nPage: Sixpence None the Richer. Sentence: Sixpence None the Richer (also known as Sixpence) is an American alternative Christian rock band that formed in New Braunfels, Texas, eventually settling in Nashville, Tennessee.\nPage: A Heavy Abacus. Sentence: \"A Heavy Abacus\" is the fifth and final single from Welsh alternative rock band The Joy Formidable's debut album \"The Big Roar\", released in July 2011.\nPage: The Joy Formidable discography. Sentence: Their debut extended play, \"A Balloon Called Moaning\", was released in December 2008, followed by their debut studio album, \"The Big Roar\", in January 2011, which reached No. 31 on the UK Albums Chart, and produced the singles \"Whirring\" and \"A Heavy Abacus\", which reached No. 7 and No. 25 on the US Alternative Songs Chart, respectively.",
